wzaes/ - WinZip AES (AE-1/AE-2) primitives for ZIP method 99.

  wzaes.c/.h: public-domain dedication (from the Xtro-ZIP unzip60
    fork). AES-CTR (counter starts at 1), PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1 with
    1000 rounds, 10-byte truncated HMAC-SHA1 over ciphertext.
    `iz_aes_decrypt` MACs the ciphertext THEN xors, so the zipread
    hook needs no separate mac_update call. `iz_aes_init` outputs
    the expected 2-byte verifier for comparison (it does not
    compare itself). Return values are int 0/1, not classic
    PKWARE booleans - check them explicitly.
  izsha1.c/.h: MIT-0, Johnsonjh (SHA-1 for PBKDF2/HMAC).
  iz_aes_x86.h, iz_arm_crypto.h, iz_arm_caps.h: supporting headers
    from the same fork. All acceleration paths are compile-time
    gated (GCC/Clang x86_64 or AArch64 only); under VC6/x86 the
    portable C path is always used.
  izsha1_ni.h: local stub - ABSENT from the upstream tree, but
    izsha1.c includes it unconditionally. Only declares the x86
    SHA-NI entry points under IZ_SHA1_NI_ENABLED, which VC6 never
    defines, so the portable C SHA-1 is always used.
  ae3_impl.h: AE-3 (AES-256-GCM) internals, compiled but unused;
    AE-3 is not a ZIP method and is not wired up.

VC6 port fixes (in wzaes.c, documented inline, behaviour-neutral):
  - `#include "izsha1.h"` added (was implicit-decl C4013 warnings).
  - `NOCRYPT` before `<windows.h>`: VC6's windows.h pulls in an
    EMPTY wincrypt.h (its contents need _WIN32_WINNT>=0x0400, which
    nothing defines) and poisons the __WINCRYPT_H__ guard, so the
    later explicit include saw nothing. Modern MSVC predefines
    _WIN32_WINNT, which is why upstream never saw this.
  - `_WIN32_WINNT` defaulted to 0x0400 (NT4, our load floor) after
    windows.h (keeps its winsock selection unchanged) so wincrypt.h
    has content. Only HCRYPTPROV/PROV_*/CRYPT_* constants are used,
    all inside iz_aes_entropy, which our decode-only DLL never
    calls; CryptoAPI stays GetProcAddress-based, so NO new static
    import is added (verified via dumpbin: KERNEL32/USER32/LZ32/
    ADVAPI32 only, unchanged).
  - `CRYPT_SILENT` (0x40) defined when missing; postdates VC6's
    wincrypt.h, same dead-code path as above.

Compiled in: wzaes.c + izsha1.c only. Both build clean under VC6
with zero warnings.

Passwords come through the existing modal dialog flow (same headless
caveat as traditional PKWARE crypto). Headless verification used
temporary password-seed/GetPassword-stub patches, both reverted
before commit (verified via git diff showing no Tool.cpp change).
